research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3360-          "source": "lem-liminf-le-limsup",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3361-          "source_section": "Statement",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3362-          "quote": "For every sequence $(x_k)$ of reals ([[def-sequence]]),\n\n$$\\liminf_{k} x_k \\;\\le\\; \\limsup_{k} x_k$$\n\nin $\\overline{\\mathbb{R}}$ ([[def-limsup-liminf]], [[def-extended-reals]]). No\nhypothesis is placed on $(x_k)$: both sides exist for every sequence\n([[lem-limsup-exists]]) and the inequality holds between them in every case,\nincluding those in which one or both sides are $\\pm\\infty$.",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3363-          "uses": [
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3364-            "4.2"
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3365-          ]
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3366-        },
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3367-        {
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3368-          "fact": "L3",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3369-          "source": "lem-of-abs-value",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3370-          "source_section": "Statement",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3371-          "quote": "Let $F$ be an ordered field ([[def-ordered-field]]) and let $x, y \\in F$, with\n$|x|$ the absolute value ([[def-abs-value]]). Then\n\n$$|x| \\ge 0; \\quad |x| = 0 \\iff x = 0; \\quad -|x| \\le x \\le |x|; \\quad |-x| = |x|; \\quad |xy| = |x|\\,|y|;$$\n\nand, for every $c > 0$, one has $|x| < c \\iff -c < x < c$.",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3372-          "uses": [
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3373-            "1.1"
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3374-          ]
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3375-        },
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3376-        {
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3377-          "fact": "L4",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json:3378:          "source": "thm-root-test",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3379-          "source_section": "Statement",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3380-          "quote": "Let $(a_k)_{k \\ge 1}$ be a family of reals from the starting index $1$\n([[def-series]]), put\n\n$$\\rho_k \\;:=\\; |a_{k+1}|^{1/(k+1)} \\qquad (k \\in \\mathbb{N}), \\qquad \\rho \\;:=\\; \\limsup_{k} \\rho_k \\;\\in\\; \\overline{\\mathbb{R}} ,$$\n\nand note that $\\rho$ exists for every such family, with no hypothesis whatever\n([[lem-limsup-exists]], [[def-limsup-liminf]]). Then:\n\n1. if $\\rho < 1$ then $\\sum_{k \\ge 1} |a_k|$ converges, and hence\n   $\\sum_{k \\ge 1} a_k$ converges as well;\n2. if $\\rho > 1$ then $\\sum_{k \\ge 1} a_k$ diverges;\n3. if $\\rho = 1$ neither conclusion follows: $\\sum_{k \\ge 1} 1/k$ diverges,\n   $\\sum_{k \\ge 1} 1/k^{2}$ converges, and both have $\\rho = 1$.\n\n**The root family is shifted, and that is forced.** The classical expression\n$|a_n|^{1/n}$ is meaningful only for $n \\ge 1$, since $1/0$ is not a rational\nnumber ([[def-rational-power]]), while sequences here are functions on\n$\\mathbb{N}$ and $\\mathbb{N}$ contains $0$. So the roots are written\n$\\rho_k = |a_{k+1}|^{1/(k+1)}$, which is $|a_n|^{1/n}$ reindexed by $n = k+1$,\nexactly the convention of [[thm-ratio-root-inequality]]. Every $\\rho_k$ is\ndefined, including where $a_{k+1} = 0$, by the supplementary clause of\n[[def-rational-power]].\n\n**What claim 1 does and does not say.** The comparison with a geometric series\ndelivers convergence of the series of *absolute values*; that\n$\\sum_{k \\ge 1} a_k$ itself converges is a separate step, and it is supplied by\n[[lem-absolute-convergence-implies-convergence]] earlier on this page. Nothing\nhere identifies the sum, and nothing here says anything about rearranging the\nseries, which is taken up later in this track.",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3381-          "uses": [
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3382-            "4.1",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3383-            "4.2",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3384-            "5.1"
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3385-          ]
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3386-        },
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3387-        {
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3388-          "fact": "L5",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3389-          "source": "thm-ratio-test",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3390-          "source_section": "Statement",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3391-          "quote": "Let $(a_k)$ be a sequence of reals with $a_k \\ne 0$ for every $k \\in \\mathbb{N}$\nand put\n\n$$q_k \\;:=\\; \\Big|\\frac{a_{k+1}}{a_k}\\Big| \\;=\\; \\frac{|a_{k+1}|}{|a_k|} \\qquad (k \\in \\mathbb{N}),$$\n\na genuine sequence on $\\mathbb{N}$, whose limit superior and limit inferior exist\nin $\\overline{\\mathbb{R}}$ for every such $(a_k)$ ([[lem-limsup-exists]]). Then:\n\n1. if $\\limsup_{k} q_k < 1$ then $\\sum |a_k|$ converges, and hence $\\sum a_k$\n   converges as well ([[lem-absolute-convergence-implies-convergence]]);\n2. if $\\liminf_{k} q_k > 1$ then $\\sum a_k$ diverges.\n\nThe hypothesis $a_k \\ne 0$ is what makes $q_k$ exist and is not a convenience: a\nsingle vanishing term leaves the ratio at that index undefined. For a family from\na starting index $m$ the statement is the one above applied to the shifted\nsequence $j \\mapsto a_{j+m}$ ([[def-series]]), whose ratios are\n$|a_{j+m+1}/a_{j+m}|$.\n\n**Nothing is claimed when $\\limsup_k q_k \\ge 1 \\ge \\liminf_k q_k$.** In that\nregime the test is silent, and it has to be: the companion page carries a\nconvergent series whose ratios have limit superior $2$, and both a convergent and\na divergent series with ratio limit exactly $1$.",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3392-          "uses": [
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3393-            "4.1",
research/audit/wave7-real-analysis-series.proof-contracts.json-3394-            "4.2",
